# UI theme

When editing menus, overlays, sheets, or dialogs under `lib/ui/`:

1. Read **`docs/UI_THEME.md`** — tokens, action hierarchy, layout escape hatches, system map.
2. **Phone-first / portrait only** (~360–430 px); tap / long-press, not hover-only.
3. Use **`GameTheme`** + **`MenuChrome`** colors/radii — no random hex (combat VFX + Kenney button palette excepted).
4. **Pick the visual family:** menu sheet (≈ GEAR) vs hub vs combat HUD vs brand vs tooltip — do not force GEAR chrome onto hub or dungeon.
5. **Action hierarchy:** one brown primary per view when possible; grey secondary; `textLink` / `ghost` for nav; red for destructive.
6. **IA copy:** RUN / TODAY / ACCOUNT — `scopeChip`, `sectionLabelScoped`, `tabBanner` for tab-owned status.
7. **Layout:** scroll, split flex, horizontal lists when content overflows — overflow stripes are bugs.
8. Actions → `KenneyButton`. Dialog cancel → `MenuChrome.dialogCancel`; +/- → `stepperButton`.
9. Press Start (`GameTheme.pixel`) for combat HUD and tiny tags only — menu body uses `body`.

English in-game copy. New shared helpers → `MenuChrome` or `KenneyButton` + one line in `docs/UI_THEME.md`.
